# Current theses

## Thesis T-migrated-sites: Preserve reviewed project guidance
Status: accepted
Based-on: user-reviewed-contract-migration

### Guidance
<folder_context path="sites">
<product_goal_and_intent name="static public documentation">
sites/git-a2a.com is the local-first static documentation and installer package for schema 2 and
the five-command CLI. It explains component code, its one responsible Agent Card, and optional
surface without presenting git-a2a as a messaging, catalog, trust, setup, MCP, or agent-hosting
product.
</product_goal_and_intent>
<system_invariant name="canonical copies">
Public install.sh is byte-identical to root install.sh. Public schema/a2amodule.v2.json and
schema/a2amodule-lock.v2.json are byte-identical to spec/schema sources. The published portable
skill tree is byte-identical to skills/git-a2a.
</system_invariant>
<settled_decision name="static local-first">
Use existing hand-written HTML/CSS/assets with no framework, analytics, remote fonts, or runtime
service. Pages work from file:// and static HTTP. Preserve responsive accessibility and brand.
</settled_decision>
<user_interface_surface name="documentation pages">
The landing page shows code dependency, owning agent card, and surface plus exactly init/add/pull/
remove/list and installation. /spec and /schema document schema 2. Remove extension/catalog/demo/
trust/MCP/setup/contact material; historical schema 1 links resolve to a migration explanation,
never a reader that suggests compatibility.
</user_interface_surface>
<compilation_and_testing_pipeline>
make site-check validates installers, strict local links, canonical copies, HTML metadata,
publication allowlist, stale-term absence, and transfer budget. Do not deploy during local work.
</compilation_and_testing_pipeline>
</folder_context>

### Rationale
Migrated from the pre-2.0 HINT source format without changing its guidance.

